Ask "How much money you start?" and call the answer balance.
Ask "How much you add every year?" and call the answer yearly.
Ask "Interest rate in percent?" and call the answer rate.
Make balance a number.
Make yearly a number.
Make rate a number.
For each year from 1 to 5:
  Add yearly to balance.
  Add balance times rate divided by 100 to balance.
  Say year followed by balance rounded to 2 decimal places.
